  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Trackpads used to reset the gesture to neutral when clicked. That's not the case anymore, but you can make that work again with some binding tweaks.\n\nIn addition to that, when you clicked on the trackpad and release the click but not the touch, it used to keep the current gesture until you stopped touching the trackpad and touched it again. That's also not the case anymore: the gesture is done instantly after the click is released, which leads to accidental gestures.\n\nTriggers used to reset the gesture to neutral  when released. That's not the case anymore, and I couldn't bring this back with binding tweaks.\n\nEdit : found a workaround for the trackpad, now it reset the gesture when clicking on it, but it still doesn't fix the gesture being done instantly if you continue touching the trackpad. https://imgur.com/mXtGnLv\n\nAlso found a workaround (thanks ZenithVal) for the trigger, but you need to fully click on the trigger to reset back to neutral. Half pressing on trigger won't reset the gesture (like before). https://imgur.com/a/s2rwiqm",
